<Base title="Known limits — Heimdall" description="What Heimdall does not do, stated up front." current="Security">
  <div class="wrap hero"><div class="eyebrow">Security</div><h1>Known, documented limits</h1>
    <p class="lede">Being upfront about what Heimdall does not do is better than letting you find out.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Rogue access point (“evil twin”) detection needs extra hardware.</strong> It works only with a second, monitor-mode WiFi adapter that you add and set up, it listens on 2.4 GHz channels 1, 6 and 11 only, and it is off until you do. See <a href="/security/wifi-monitor/">WiFi monitor</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>On an ordinary switch, Heimdall does not see other devices’ private traffic.</strong> Its sniff interface hears broadcast and multicast and its own machine’s traffic. Suricata and Zeek see more only if the switch or router mirrors traffic to Heimdall’s port.</li>
      <li><strong>Incoming port scans are not detected.</strong> Heimdall’s nightly scan runs outward against devices it already knows.</li>
      <li><strong>Encrypted DNS and TLS downloads bypass inspection.</strong> Only cleartext DNS on port 53 is inspected, and no TLS interception is configured, so encrypted downloads never reach ClamAV.</li>
      <li><strong>Suricata’s rule set is unmanaged.</strong> Expect noise until you tune it.</li>
      <li><strong>Wired traffic is per port, not per device</strong>, because routers only count per port. Heimdall labels it PORT TOTAL.</li>
      <li><strong>Block and quarantine depend on your router.</strong> Many adapters cannot do either; passive mode cannot.</li>
      <li><strong>Only two routers have been tested on real hardware.</strong> See <a href="/equipment/">the equipment table</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Alpha software.</strong> Built and tested on one home network.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">A penetration-test plan covering every capability and every gap above is in the repository: <a href="https://github.com/danielonet/heimdall/blob/main/docs/testing/heimdall_verification.md">docs/testing/heimdall_verification.md</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
